{"availability":"available","full":"isladjan/particles-playground","name":"particles-playground","description":"A WebGL project driven by particles, built with Three.js and GSAP. It creates dynamic, animated visuals with smooth effects and interactive motion.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":23,"forks":4,"created":"2025-01-08T19:55:03Z","updated":"2025-01-08T23:43:52Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://isladjan.com/work/3/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T05:01:32.879Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T05:01:32.879Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T05:01:32.879Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:44:05.971Z","stars":22,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-13T04:12:41.123Z","stars":23,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-19T05:01:32.879Z","stars":23,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A WebGL project driven by particles, built with Three.js and GSAP. The particles are constructed using custom shaders and utilize image textures as the base for coloring and rendering their appearance.","Custom shaders handle particle behavior, transforming images into interactive displays. It supports dynamic effects like texture transitions, mouse and touch interactions, and a flowing \"tail\" effect for interaction with particles. Performance is optimized with FPS limiting and throttled events.","This project utilizes GLSL 2D simplex noise within the shaders, originally developed by Ian McEwan. This project is inspired by Bruno Imbrizi's Interactive Particles."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/isladjan/particles-playground/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"94fc877d385eb320213c0b5e49562f0ed12aea382cc76f28ed8361a144b582e7","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:06.064Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:44:06.064Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A WebGL project driven by particles, built with Three.js and GSAP. The particles are constructed using